  "interpretation": [
    "APU RAM 0x03D5-0x1527 is a strong shared audio-driver/code candidate because it is byte-identical across all ten snapshots and every captured SPC program counter lies inside it.",
    "APU RAM 0x3000-0x5F87 is the beginning of a shared BRR sample bank: every snapshot uses the sample directory at 0xFF00 and valid sample data begins at 0x3000.",
    "Unused Song 1 is structurally aligned with Demo Race: 87.4512% APU-RAM identity, with all 19 valid BRR samples shared at the same indices.",
    "Unused Song 2 is structurally aligned with the numbered-race family: all 24 valid BRR samples occur at the same indices in every numbered race, with about 88.8-89.0% APU-RAM identity.",
    "The two large shared APU ranges do not appear verbatim in the canonical USA ROM, so CPU-side upload/decompression/transformation remains to be located.",
    "These findings classify audio-state families; they do not prove why the unused compositions are unreachable in retail gameplay."
  ]
